.TH geectl-maintenance-maintenance-branch 1  "geectl-maintenance-maintenance-branch 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-maintenance\-maintenance\-branch \- Branch a maintained package into its maintenance branch project and report where it landed. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); the global `\-\-live` performs the branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl maintenance maintenance\-branch\fR [\fB\-\-attribute\fR] [\fB\-\-update\-project\-attribute\fR] [\fB\-\-target\-project\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-package\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Branch a maintained package into its maintenance branch project and report where it landed. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); the global `\-\-live` performs the branch
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
The package to branch into its maintenance branch project
.TP
\fB\-\-attribute\fR \fI<ATTRIBUTE>\fR
The attribute marking a project as maintaining the package (`NAMESPACE:NAME`, default `OBS:Maintained`)
.TP
\fB\-\-update\-project\-attribute\fR \fI<UPDATE_PROJECT_ATTRIBUTE>\fR
The attribute pointing a project at its update project (`NAMESPACE:NAME`, default `OBS:UpdateProject`)
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
Override the server\-derived branch project (`home:<user>:branches:OBS_Maintained:<package>`)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
